        "Body": {
          "ContentType": "html",
          "Content": "<div><span><span></span></span><br></div><div><p><span><span>In</span></span><span><span><span>&nbsp;</span></span></span><span><span>early November</span><span><span>&nbsp;</span>2025</span></span><span><span>, the following updates and enhancements were made to Azure SQL:</span></span><span>&nbsp;</span><span>&nbsp;</span></p></div><ul><li><p><span><span>Azure SQL Hyperscale now supports multiple geo-secondary replicas, making it easier to design and deploy disaster recovery topology spanning multiple regions.<span>&nbsp;</span></span></span><a href=\"https://aka.ms/sqlhsmultisecondary\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span><span><span>Learn more</span></span></span></a><span><span>.</span></span><span>&nbsp;</span></p></li><li><p><span><span>Azure SQL Database<span>&nbsp;</span></span><span>enables<span>&nbsp;</span></span><span>you<span>&nbsp;</span></span><span>to restart your database in the Azure portal</span><span>.&nbsp;<span>&nbsp;</span></span><span>The portal uses the same API that is available for PowerShell,<span>&nbsp;</span></span><span>REST</span></span><span><span><span>,</span></span></span><span><span><span>&nbsp;</span>and Az</span></span><span><span><span>ure</span></span></span><span><span><span>&nbsp;</span>CLI.&nbsp;<span>&nbsp;</span></span></span><a href=\"https://aka.ms/sqlrestart\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span><span><span>Learn more</span></span></span></a><span><span>.&nbsp;</span></span><span>&nbsp;</span></p></li></ul>",
          "Markdown": "In early November 2025 , the following updates and enhancements were made to Azure SQL:\n\nAzure SQL Hyperscale now supports multiple geo-secondary replicas, making it easier to design and deploy disaster recovery topology spanning multiple regions. Learn more .\n\nAzure SQL Database enables you to restart your database in the Azure portal . The portal uses the same API that is available for PowerShell, REST , and Az ure CLI. Learn more ."
        },
